582
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:41,440
As for the set of tools we use for programming and development afterwards,

583
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:46,320
what we use is the version listed right here.

584
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:51,480
Actually, the whole instruction set is split into, you could say, two parts or two volumes.

585
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:54,100
One volume is called the unprivileged instructions.

586
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:59,300
That is what is written here as unprivileged,

587
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:01,080
meaning the unprivileged instructions.

588
